Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-23
Subject: Guard cgcpu's Windows stack-probe asm with $ifndef NOTARGETWIN32
License: expat

`compiler/i386/cgcpu.pas` carries a Windows-specific stack-page-probing
sequence -- Win32 only commits a few stack pages, so the prologue has
to touch every later page before using it. The block is gated by
`{$ifndef __NOWINPECOFF__}`, but the inner `target_info.system =
system_i386_win32` arm still references Win32 target metadata.

The bootstrap is built `-dNOTARGETWIN32`. Add an `{$ifndef
NOTARGETWIN32}` around that arm so the bootstrap doesn't drag any of
the Win32 target plumbing (system identifiers, related target info)
into the tp2cc runtime.

--- a/compiler/i386/cgcpu.pas
+++ b/compiler/i386/cgcpu.pas
@@ -330,6 +330,7 @@
 {$ifndef __NOWINPECOFF__}
         { windows guards only a few pages for stack growing, }
         { so we have to access every page first              }
+{$ifndef NOTARGETWIN32}
         if target_info.system=system_i386_win32 then
           begin
              objectlibrary.getlabel(again);
@@ -359,6 +360,7 @@
              end;
           end
         else
+{$endif NOTARGETWIN32}
 {$endif __NOWINPECOFF__}
           list.concat(Taicpu.op_reg_reg(A_SUB,S_L,NR_EDI,NR_ESP));
        { align stack on 4 bytes }
